# Arches fleet C++ style: 4-space indent, access specifiers aligned with
# members, pointers/references attach to the type (const std::string& x).
#
# Byte-identical to Arches-Client/.clang-format. The fleet had three answers to
# this question and two repos with no answer at all: Client was LLVM/100,
# Arches-Instrumentation is Microsoft/300 (deliberately, for its own reasons --
# see the rationale in that file), and HAL and Server had no .clang-format, so
# clang-format silently fell back to plain LLVM at 80 columns. Their gates run
# `clang-format --dry-run --Werror` against that fallback and were failing on
# it. See Task.md G-02.
BasedOnStyle: LLVM
IndentWidth: 4
ColumnLimit: 100
DerivePointerAlignment: false
PointerAlignment: Left
AccessModifierOffset: 0
